---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="mdbase Connect"
  description="Host and synchronize Markdown collections, serve local folders to applications, and control access through explicit permissions."
  current="connect"
>
  <section class="content-section" aria-label="About mdbase Connect">
    <h1 class="sr-only">mdbase Connect</h1>
    <p>
      mdbase Connect makes Markdown collections available to applications. It
      hosts collections online, synchronizes them with local copies, and
      manages application access.
    </p>
    <p>
      When a collection is hosted, Connect serves its online copy directly.
      When a collection remains on your computer, the mdbase Connector serves
      the folder locally. Connect still manages approval, but the contents of
      local operations do not pass through the hosted service.
    </p>
    <p>
      Connect encrypts hosted collections in transit and at rest. Because the
      service serves those files to approved applications, it can decrypt
      hosted records while processing requests. The <a href="/security/"
        >security documentation</a
      > explains this boundary in more detail.
    </p>
    <p>
      When an application asks for access, you choose a collection and review
      what it needs to do. The permission applies only to that application and
      collection and can be narrowed, paused, or revoked later.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can <a href="/downloads/">download the Connector</a> to use local
      folders, <a href="/beta/">create a Connect account</a> for hosted
      collections, or <a href="https://connect.mdbase.dev/login">sign in</a> to
      manage an existing account.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
